# Mutations for mutate.py. Each one swaps a piece of SpawnPool.tla for a
# plausible bug and names the one property that must fail on it. The text
# after `- ` must occur exactly once in the spec; `+ ` lines replace it. An
# optional `only <label-substring>` line limits the matrix runs. Every property
# the matrix checks needs a mutation.

# The calling code before it polled the worker processes.
mutation parent never polls for a dead worker
detects Closed
only items=1
- Poll == (\E w \in W : worker[w] = "dead") /\ Abort
+ Poll == FALSE /\ Abort

mutation worker keeps its job after handing it over
detects Own
-     /\ job' = [job EXCEPT ![w] = 0]
-     /\ worker' = [worker EXCEPT ![w] = state]
+     /\ job' = job
+     /\ worker' = [worker EXCEPT ![w] = state]

mutation finished worker enters an unknown state
detects TypeOK
- Finish(w) == Leave(w, "ok", "idle")
+ Finish(w) == Leave(w, "ok", "broken")

mutation parent records the last item instead of the next one
detects Order
- delivered' = Append(delivered, i)
+ delivered' = Append(delivered, Items)

mutation parent closes without waiting for its workers
detects NoLeak
- Join == /\ pc = "join"
-         /\ \A w \in W : worker[w] = "closed"
+ Join == /\ pc = "join"
